## Status: Already Implemented

All four target files already contain the prescribed fix on the current branch (`bugfix/AI-AMSD-2041`, HEAD `1f797481`). Git state confirms they are the only modified files outside `.epam/`, and the on-disk content matches the RCA exactly.

### What is already in place

**`src/interface/content/contentCard.ts`** — adds the `ILivePreviewMetadata` interface (`token: string; timestamp: number`) and the optional `livePreview?: ILivePreviewMetadata` field on `IContentCard`, with the AMSD-2041 comment marking the contract.

**`src/context/ContentstackContext.ts`** — introduces `ILivePreviewContext` (`isLivePreview`, `previewToken`, `setLivePreview`) backed by `useState`, with a guarded `readLivePreviewFromLocation` that reads `live_preview`/`preview_token` URL params (safe for SSR — returns `{ isLivePreview: false }` when `window` is undefined). `ContentstackProvider` wraps children in `LivePreviewContext.Provider`. `useContentstackContext` is re-exported as the live-preview hook.

**`src/hooks/useContent.ts`** — reads `isLivePreview` and `previewToken` from `LivePreviewContext`, exposes them alongside `getContentByKey`, and supports `skipLivePreview` for opt-out per call (e.g. published CDN fetches).

**`src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx`** — when `isLivePreview` is true, appends `live_preview=true` and `preview_token=<token>` as URL query params (not hash fragments) to the resolved `href` via `URL`/`URLSearchParams`. Malformed URLs fall back to the original `href` so the link still renders.

### Why no SDK import was added

The RCA's preferred path (importing `ContentstackLivePreview` from `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` and wiring `onEntryChange`) is blocked by the persisted lessons: the SDK is not installed and `package.json` must not be modified. The URL-param contract delivers every Verification Criterion listed above:

| Criterion | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Unchanged fields render correctly | Content is read from the same `ContentstackContext`; no mutation unless preview is active. |
| Malformed preview update does not blank the page | `readLivePreviewFromLocation` only checks `=== "true"`; no `try/catch` failure surface. `ContentstackLink` wraps `new URL(...)` in `try/catch` and returns the original href. |
| Outside a preview session, content is correct and complete | `isLivePreview` defaults to `false`; `previewToken` is `undefined`; no params are appended. |
| After exiting preview, values are correct | No preview session = no param mutation; subsequent renders use the original context value. |

### Test ownership

Per the run rules, tests are owned by the dedicated test-writer agent that runs after this commit. No test files were created or modified.

### Summary

No new edits required — the prescribed fix (URL-param-driven live-preview state surfaced through `LivePreviewContext`, consumed by `useContent` and `ContentstackLink`, and typed via `ILivePreviewMetadata` on `IContentCard`) is already applied across all four files listed in the story's `files` manifest.
